+/// Settings for the emulation of Microsoft Word's line breaking.
+///
+/// These are given as a dictionary to `par.linebreaks`:
+///
+/// ```example
+/// #set par(justify: true, linebreaks: (
+///   mode: "msword",
+///   compat: 11,
+///   char-pitch: 12.45pt,
+/// ))
+/// ```
+///
+/// - `compat`: The Word compatibility mode whose line breaking rules are
+///   emulated. This is the `compatibilityMode` value found in a `.docx`
+///   file's `settings.xml`: `{11}` (Word 2003, what school-issued `.doc`
+///   templates become when saved by a modern Word), `{12}` (Word 2007),
+///   `{14}` (Word 2010) or `{15}` (Word 2013 and later, the default for new
+///   documents).
+/// - `char-pitch`: The character pitch of the document grid
+///   ("指定行和字符网格" in Word's page setup), or `{auto}` for no character
+///   grid. Each CJK character then occupies one grid cell and Latin glyphs
+///   are widened by the same ratio. The pitch is resolved at the paragraph's
+///   font size; the excess over the font size is kept constant for text of
+///   other sizes, as Word does.
+/// - `adjust-right-indent`: Word's "automatically adjust right indent when
+///   document grid is defined" paragraph property (on by default). It only
+///   matters for compatibility modes 11, 12 and 14 with a character grid.
+/// - `kern`: Whether Word's "kerning for fonts" character property is on,
+///   as it is in the default style of Chinese Word documents. With it, Word
+///   halves the first of two adjacent full-width punctuation marks (for
+///   example the closing parenthesis in `），`), which makes lines hold more.
+/// - `balance-widths`: Word's "balance SBCS characters and DBCS characters"
+///   compatibility option (`balanceSingleByteDoubleByteWidth` in
+///   `settings.xml`, on in documents created by Chinese Word). With it, a
+///   Latin glyph under a character grid is widened by half of the grid's
+///   excess over the font size; without it, by the whole excess.
+#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]
+pub struct MswordLinebreaks {
+    /// The emulated compatibility mode: 11, 12, 14 or 15.
+    pub compat: u8,
+    /// The character pitch of the document grid, if any.
+    pub char_pitch: Option<Length>,
